    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66-a6">

                <pb facs="0999" n="989" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv03/pg989"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram, General Nudant to Etat-Major
                    Bacon</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 496</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">From <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Spa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-27"
                            >27 January, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Reply to Telegram No. 3564/C.R.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>The German Government is ready in principle to allow food destined for
                        Poland (of the Congress) to pass. But it seems doubtful whether the bad
                        condition of the railways and the great shortage of rolling stock will
                        permit of the flow of traffic without hindrance as far as the German-Polish
                        frontier.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Germany asks to be assured that the material supplied for the transport of
                        these provisions shall be immediately returned.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>The German Commission reserves to itself the right of making other
                        communications on this subject later on.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
